  "description": "Bean qou-prjo. Asks whether q_cross(n) \u2014 the q at which the \u0394_\u03bb-weighted \u22653-row archimedean trace changes sign \u2014 is a STRUCTURED SEQUENCE, and whether q\u2080's position in it is DERIVED or COINCIDENTAL. Establishes three branch-geometry facts first: (BG-1) the y_\u03bb normaliser is the closed form Z=((1\u2212Q^r)/(1\u2212Q))^n by dual Cauchy, and is positive on (1,q*), so it can neither create nor destroy a crossing; (BG-2) the Wenzl level eigenvalue Q^r=u\u00b3/(\u2212u\u2076\u2212u\u2074+u\u00b3+u\u00b2+1) (u=\u221aq) has a POLE at q*=1.278449576579693\u2026, above which the effective level r is COMPLEX \u2014 so the real-level branch is (1,q*) and the previously-reported n=9 crossings at q\u22481.43/1.46 lie OFF it; (BG-3) at integer level r=k every \u03bb with \u2113(\u03bb)>k has s_\u03bb=0, giving the level-integer ladder q_k (explicit integer polynomial) which increases and accumulates at q*, with q\u2080 strictly inside (q_2,q_3)=(1,1.15416\u2026). On the real-level branch the crossing set is computed for the character-free G_n (n=3..N) and the character-dressed F_K (D,T,\u00b3He,\u2074He, including the n=12 \u2074He leg left open by #4829). Crossings are shown EXACTLY ALGEBRAIC (irreducible integer minimal polynomial in u=\u221aq, certified real-root isolation). A GENERICITY GATE then measures the width of the interval around q\u2080 that reproduces the same sign pattern, in absolute terms, as a fraction of the branch, in bits, and by counting systematically-generated natural constants inside it. \u0394_\u03bb=(\u22121)^{n(\u03bb)}\u00b7dim is the PROVED value-only weight; free_parameters=0; AME never used; experimental proton anchor; layer-pure; live y_\u03bb closed form, NOT the muon cache.",
